{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Then the land shall be appeased.</b> Then, when there pass over you the six decrees in the matters that we mentioned — measure for measure, such as: six years that you had to work it, and in the seventh to cease — then the land shall be appeased regarding its sabbaths. That is, it will remember and lament over its former custom, that it would work the six years and rest in the seventh." "<b>תרצה.</b> It will remember, as in ״ואחריהם בפיהם ירצו״ — which is like יזכירו. Another interpretation: <b>תרצה</b> — it will complete, as in ״עד ירצה כשכיר יומו״, ״כי נרצה עונה״, and likewise <b>והרצת את שבתותיה.</b> Another interpretation: <b>אז תרצה הארץ</b> — the land shall be reconciled, as in ״ולא יוסיף לרצות עוד״ and ״ומשביע לכל חי רצון״, and likewise ״והרצת״ (25) <b>את שבתותיה</b> — that it did not rest in them." "<b>Then the land shall rest.</b> With pataḥ."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:41.869114864Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}